{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1167667-pro-s-of-an-invictus-prince","id":1167667,"title":"Pro's of an Invictus Prince","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-14T09:03:24-08:00","id":1167667,"title":"Pro's of an Invictus Prince","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I'm trying to push the concept of a good old fashioned princedom on a domain in a large scale game. Currently, we're run by a Carthian experiment council and things are slow as shit. Everything goes through the council and so Council meetings take forever and tie up multiple players valuable time and keeps them from taking on the positions where they can be most useful. (I am the Invictus Primogen, newly moving into this role as a social character.)<br /> <br /> I would like to find an IC way to push for a much smaller government that preferably doesn't antagonize the Carthian's too much as I actually have a fairly good relationship with several of them. Antics of other covenants have sort of united us on that front.<br /> <br /> My current idea is to try and get the council to agree to endorsing a prince (I think I have the votes already if some sort of catalyst event were to occur to justify it.) I have the military power, but not the social power in that regard. My idea would be to promise to delegate the responsibility properly to different positions - stop requiring votes on everything the Sheriff or Harpies did, etc.<br /> <br /> I guess, what I'm asking for is ideas of what sort of nod to the Carthian's I can put in place for a new traditional style government that would work to ease their concerns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T09:30:43-08:00","id":1167677,"title":"","content":"Well, you could structure it as &quot;let me get shit done&quot; with the Carthian council having veto and law making powers. Basically, the Prince can do what needs to be done, provided it breaks no Laws, and the Council doesn't say &quot;nope&quot; afterwards.<br /> <br /> Asking forgiveness, as oppossed to permission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T10:17:03-08:00","id":1167691,"title":"","content":"My favorite pro of an Invictus Prince? <br /> <br /> If the Prince uses Invicstus Oaths with all the citizens, they literally get benefits for being the subjects. Its a win-win situation. You could get free disciplines, or free blood, whatever. Very handy.<br /> Invictus leaders tend to be very good at their jobs - remmeber that the Estate is a meritocracy, so you know that the guy earned his way up.<br /> An invictus prince wants to be in power - and that means that they're willing to play ball with every covenant, irregardless of which one, if it means they get to stay in power. An Invictus Prince could very well go out of their way to arrange a balance of power between all five covenants so that the city is relavitely stable with him or her on top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T12:26:15-08:00","id":1167741,"title":"","content":"The best form of government is an enlightened, benevolent monarchy. The worst is a monarchy undergoing a transfer of power. Avoid the transfer of power and you have strong arguments that things will work better, peace be maintained, and the flow of resources will increase.<br /> <br /> In your case you have a council that consists of the petty fiefdoms of everyone on it. They will not gladly release power, however they could deputize an agent (you) to Get Crap Done in several very specific ways. You as agent must argue that you cannot spend all your time going back to the council for every decision before taking action--or there's no point. You have to have the ability to do stuff, then discuss afterwards and if you act within the boundaries agreed by the Council in advance you will not be held in censure. <br /> <br /> As a Carthian domain your city operates under the effects of Carthian Law--which is handy and useful. You, as Prince-Agent could tap that by making certain requests of the Council to enact Law beneficial to the domain overall. Meanwhile, as an Invictus, you have at your disposal Oaths that enable you to demonstrate the rightness of an ordered society as you spread them from a position of authority.<br /> <br /> You only need to acquire <i>enough</i> authority to then deputize your own agents (Notary, Sheriff, etc.). You'll have more trouble bringing the Harpies into your orbit, but that's what the Oaths are for: you can use them as both carrot and stick to specifically help them out. You may choose to agree with the Council that no members of that body may be deputized by you... but then you can work around that by deputizing their subordinates, which both undercuts control by a given Council member, gives that member an &quot;in&quot; to your circle, and rewards them and the deputy. <br /> <br /> Ultimately your goal is to arrange just enough Council in-fighting to whittle down its membership until you have every single member well under your control. Control that they are <i>happy</i> to have over them, mind you. Along the way, just enough smaller &quot;fires&quot; can occur to pass more and more authority directly to you as Prince-Agent, that you can dispense with the &quot;agent&quot; part. Essentially you need your Reichstag fire to get the Council to agree to the scheme, you need to demonstrate (quickly) the benefits of yourself as prince, and then you need a few new crises that don't link to you to harm Council members and get them to agree to give you more power/autonomy.<br /> <br /> Councils are suspicious things; if not they'd be more efficient. Avoid directing that suspicion onto yourself and you'll succeed.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T14:40:59-08:00","id":1167776,"title":"","content":"You could always this age-old government powegrab technique, famously used by Julius Caesar as well as a wide variety of taxes and other exploitative laws.<br /> <br /> First, manufacture some crisis. A brewing war with the warewolves or mages, or a rash of domain invasions and feeding violations by outsider Kindred. Then you kindly but assertively declare &quot;I can fix this! I have a plan! Only I have the knowledge and experience to get this fixed before it destroys us all! If you all just grant me some <i>temporary</i> power to get all this sorted out and then I'll <i>gladly</i> return when those Outsiders have been dealt with and we can all go back to living in *cough* peace!&quot;<br /> Of course in government, any temporary concentration of power is quickly used to further concentrate power and make it all permanent. The crisis(es) never actually gets solved, something destabilizes or distracts the opposition, deadlines get missed etc etc.<br /> I/We just need a little <i>more</i> power, <i>more</i> time, and <i>more</i> resources then everything will be great again! Come ahhhn, have I/we ever let you down before? You know that I/we have a long track record of trustworthiness.<br /> <br /> Then after some time has passed, you say &quot;Look how great this has been going! It's been like this forever and things have improved sooo much that we should keep it this way. See this group of people who agree!&quot; (And if <i>you</i> don't, then they just might help you mysteriously meet the sun then discover your hastily written suicide note)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 12-14-2017, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T16:17:29-08:00","id":1167790,"title":"","content":"Though those strategies can work, it is wise to keep some things in mind. First, that this council is formed by some old undead monsters, so they probably can get the gist of what is happening and not be so easy to fool. Second, that as Carthians they are already versed both in being cautious with the Invictus MO and trying new approaches.<br /> <br /> You should start with considering the individuals with more power on this council. Their experience, or lack thereof, as their personal opinions can inform much of the best strategies. Then it could be interesting to try to not go straight against them. Evaluate the best approach for each, take into account their own agendas, and mainly focus on building over their organization without trying to negate it, it is their precious social experiment.<br /> <br /> At last, evaluate your own ambition. What do you want? You want all the power to yourself? You want to have some job done? You just want to be influential and well fed in a solid organization? If you have a clear goal, the next step is to plan the way there. Get a note of what you need to be at the position, and then break the way up there in smaller, more manageable goals. Repeat until you have a clear but versatile path to your final goal.<br /> <br /> Don't try to plan precise methods of arriving there, instead focus on positions. Killing counselor X isn't a plan, but to become assistant to a counselor is. Avoid advancement that seems too good now, but take you away from your path, unless you want to change your goals. Prepare for each advancement eagerly, but don't try to overstep, it can be dangerous. Be patient, bide your time. If you play well, you'll have all the time you need to get there, and all the time you want to bask in the results. If you take a false step, though, you can put everything to lose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T16:20:10-08:00","id":1167791,"title":"","content":"Here's something that I found interesting one of the old writers said. Don't remember if it was David Hill, or Rose, or some one else. But, here it is: The new covenants are designed for each person to have a reason to have the others stick around. <br /> <br /> In 1e, there was little reason not to destroy any opposing covenants the moment they reared their head. Now? Now an Invictus Prince is going to look at a Carthian Senshel, and realize that they're practically immune to mind fuckery if the Prince gives them a bit of slack and plays Carthian Law to his advantage. She wants the Lawyers around for the benefits they bring to his table. He's going to see the Lance and see their expertise in tracking and hunting offenders (making great sheriffs and hounds), and see the diviners of the Crone and how they benefit the domain with their foresight. She'll look at the Ordo and their abilty to heal wounds on vampires and remove bonds and other unique tricks. <br /> <br /> Every covenant brings something to the table to help make a rather stable society overall. With the Invictus, its protection of the masquerade and its abiilty to strengthen and empower any retainers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T04:35:22-08:00","id":1167865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1167667-pro-s-of-an-invictus-prince?p=1167691#post1167691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An invictus prince wants to be in power - and that means that they're willing to play ball with every covenant, irregardless of which one, if it means they get to stay in power. An Invictus Prince could very well go out of their way to arrange a balance of power between all five covenants so that the city is relavitely stable with him or her on top.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another factor that tends in the same direction is that the Invictus above all wants a domain to be <i>calm</i>. And that means finding a way to make disruptive influences not - sure you could do that with force, but force is noisy too, and has echoes - better to give them something they want instead or at least as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T05:42:17-08:00","id":1167879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1167667-pro-s-of-an-invictus-prince?p=1167791#post1167791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every covenant brings something to the table to help make a rather stable society overall. With the Invictus, its protection of the masquerade and its abiilty to strengthen and empower any retainers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you hit the nail on the head here. A lot of people are going evil dictator, but there's room for the benevolent dictators too - the Invictus Prince who sees the Carthian experiment as an excuse to run the domain as a boardroom rather than a fiefdom. I'm leaning towards selling the Carthian's as the 'checks and balances' of the government - the ones who essentially ensure that power cant be abused. It'll be abused anyways, but hopefully to a lesser extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T07:26:23-08:00","id":1167904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1167667-pro-s-of-an-invictus-prince?p=1167879#post1167879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you hit the nail on the head here. A lot of people are going evil dictator, but there's room for the benevolent dictators too - the Invictus Prince who sees the Carthian experiment as an excuse to run the domain as a boardroom rather than a fiefdom. I'm leaning towards selling the Carthian's as the 'checks and balances' of the government - the ones who essentially ensure that power cant be abused. It'll be abused anyways, but hopefully to a lesser extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly: hence my recommendation to approach the situation as something that can be structured as an assistance to the Council. If you find that that structure does not feed your power needs, then breaking things down to a more directly neo-feudal arrangement is feasible if not straightforward in theory. <br /> <br /> English history actually provides several examples of strong councils working with (and, opposing) kings. The key to succeeding, at least in the early phase, will be to ensure that the unilateral actions as Prince align with the mandates provided and demonstrate good faith worthy of further trust. In other words, that you're a responsible Agent.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T09:12:56-08:00","id":1167936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1167667-pro-s-of-an-invictus-prince?p=1167879#post1167879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you hit the nail on the head here. A lot of people are going evil dictator, but there's room for the benevolent dictators too - the Invictus Prince who sees the Carthian experiment as an excuse to run the domain as a boardroom rather than a fiefdom. I'm leaning towards selling the Carthian's as the 'checks and balances' of the government - the ones who essentially ensure that power cant be abused. It'll be abused anyways, but hopefully to a lesser extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Carthians are good at coming up with stuff. The Invictus use what works, sometimes at the cost of coming up with more. That means the Carthians can be useful to a savvy Invictus - because some of what they come up with will work, and Invictus long for this world won't discard a good idea because of where it comes from - and has something to offer them in getting their ideas into a power structure more of the other covenants are likely to trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T16:02:44-08:00","id":1168039,"title":"","content":"The Invictus use whatever they can get their hands on. There's a reason why the keepers of the Masquerade are the most tech saavy of the five covenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T23:03:33-08:00","id":1168132,"title":"","content":"<br /> Don't ask for a princedom, they will say no and be offended. You make THEM ask for a princedom.<br /> <br /> What you want to do is reform the government.<br /> <br /> Make people dislike the current form of government enough that you can get away with adding a 'minor' change to it to centralize power. Show off the centralized(president, mayor, speaker of the Parliament etc) power being strong and scary and respectable. Make people want more of it. When a problem falls into the councils hands make the public think they are going to screw up. Let people think any success the council has is because of the centralized power and not the council.<br /> <br /> With enough discontent towards the council get your cronies to spread the idea of the council being lower or separate from the centralized power. Let the people vote on it.<br /> <br /> Your goal is to split the two and keep them equal, or make the council advise/regulate the centralized power. Remember don't goose step in, you gotta take it slow.<br /> <br /> Step by step you distance the council from importance and relevance while assuming power yourself and in the centralized power. Introduce Invictus shit latter down the line when people are more open to it. The big thing is reading the room.<br /> <br /> Things to help you achieve this;<ul><li>Ever wonder what the Staff merit was for? Have Staff:Kindred Gossipers(Expression) tell tales of the councils incompetence around town. You can find places more open to ideas and harder nuts to crack by how well these guys work in an area. Staff:Ghoul Firebrand(Persuasion) should camp outside places kindred gather to convince people of your goals and intentions. The big thing to remember is to avoid leaving these guys working in places with competition. Get a monopoly on the head space and let your minions do the work.</li> <li>Bribes. Never underestimate the equipment bonus from giving people exactly what they want. You want the council to appear weak or incompetent, not you. It doesn't need to be coin but you need people to think &quot;If I stand with this guy, good things will happen to me&quot; even when your about to throw them in the fire. Avoid murder, breaking the masquerade and other socially unforgivable shit. Its too expensive to deal with, if something like that has to be done then do it by proxies proxy.</li> <li>Not talking. Don't stay in the room alone with a mind reader. When you do something don't tell people about it who might get upset. If you get seen helping someone at the expense of another admit to helping that person but don't give a reason why. If they push the subject and they are better at social(or evenly matched, anything beyond you stomping them at least) then you then claim your being framed and storm out. Remember the second point; you want people to like you and come to your aid. Your foes are their foes. Keep people from wanting to attack you in any official fashion. People with good empathy will know you are telling the truth(as well as bad empathy...usually) but hiding something. As long as you don't fully explain yourself then you won't get captured in an outright lie. The goal isn't to be a saint, but the least hated person in the room. Its better to be everyones second choice rather then half the rooms first choice.</li> <li>Allies and contact. The hard part. You need enough power that you can control the council but you have to keep your allies from amassing too much power without your permission, rendering you pointless and your plans a failure.You have to keep them loyal and in balance with each other. Have contacts within their enemies so you can get a heads up on what they are doing and not telling you and work to turn their attacks to your benefit. The goal is to keep both sides fighting with no one winning until you make your new council, then use your contacts to surgically strike your foe and achieve victory.</li> </ul>Well thats an idea anyway. You could always invite the Invictus into town and scheme your way into control of the council and then install a prince then. That should be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11660-sleepychicken","name":"SleepyChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11660_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T03:03:41-08:00","id":1168145,"title":"","content":"How big is this council? If it consists of every vampire in the domain argue that it is an unreasonable tax on the time of the common kindred, if it's quite small then by it's very existence it proves that power is best held by a competent elite. Also who can sit on the council? That could make some strategies more or less likely to work.<br /> Argue that democracy doesn't produce good government it makes removing bad government easier, as long as the council has the ability to remove the Prince there's no problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}